    {
      "type": "CommentNode",
      "width": 260,
      "height": 270,
      "position": {
        "x": 1110,
        "y": 470
      },
      "text": "While composition\\ncould also be\\npossible, conditions\\ncan exist elsewhere\\nso I found aggregation\\nmore applicable.\\nIt depends on if we're talking\\nin general, or about a\\nspecific condition, where the\\nlifetime of the condition would\\nequal that of the while loop, and\\ncomposition (indicating that the\\ncondition should be destroyed\\nwhen the while loop is) would\\nbe more accurate.",
      "hasDoubleBorder": false,
      "styleObject": {
        "fill": "white",
        "stroke": "black",
        "stroke-width": 2,
        "fill-opacity": 1,
        "stroke-opacity": 0.75
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "CommentNode",
      "width": 240,
      "height": 90,
      "position": {
        "x": 1120,
        "y": 750
      },
      "text": "Same idea as previous.\\nHere I assumed the opposite\\n(specific case, not general)",
      "hasDoubleBorder": false,
      "styleObject": {
        "fill": "white",
        "stroke": "black",
        "stroke-width": 2,
        "fill-opacity": 1,
        "stroke-opacity": 0.75
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "CommentNode",
      "width": 310,
      "height": 120,
      "position": {
        "x": 1380,
        "y": 550
      },
      "text": "It's the same as the difference\\nwhen describing it in natural\\nlanguage; a while loop has a condition\\nbut this specific condition x is part of\\nthis while loop. Hard to say which is more\\naccurate without knowing the context\\nof the system being designed",
      "hasDoubleBorder": false,
      "styleObject": {
        "fill": "white",
        "stroke": "black",
        "stroke-width": 2,
        "fill-opacity": 1,
        "stroke-opacity": 0.75
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "CommentNode",
      "width": 310,
      "height": 60,
      "position": {
        "x": 1380,
        "y": 680
      },
      "text": "Hard not to sound argumentative,\\nbut to clear it up I am just explaining my\\nmotivation in hopes of getting the points",
